# Golden bytes: network NBT for the text component {"text":"bye"}.
#
# **Checked against real network NBT**, which it had never been. A vanilla 26.1.2 server, told to `say bye` on
# its console with a client connected, sends:
#
#   08 00 03 62 79 65  05 08 00 06 53 65 72 76 65 72  00
#   ^TAG_String ^len3 "bye" ...
#
# -- the same encoding this file uses for its string entry: tag type `08`, a two-byte name length, UTF-8
# payload. Vanilla wrote the **bare-string** form of the component and this fixture writes the **compound**
# form; both are valid, and the encoding they share is what the test exercises.
# 0A                compound
#   08 0004 "text"  string entry named text
#   0003 "bye"      string payload
# 00                end
0A
08 00 04 74 65 78 74
00 03 62 79 65
00
